[routes]
GET /relay-worker.js          → 200 text/javascript, the page's service worker

[commands]

[pages]
/telling                      the telling page: the control, and the address once on
main[data-telling-state]      unasked | on | off | refused | unanswered
#ask                          asks the device to allow the telling
#ask[data-state]              "ready", or "asking" while the ask is open
#stop                         stops the telling; present only while on
#endpoint                     the address the device was given; present only while on
#why                          why the telling is not on, when it is not

[files]

[notes]
the page holds nothing server-side: the state it wears comes from what
the browser tells it, so a reload re-reads the subscription rather than
being handed it. the service worker is fetched on every load.
